content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 85 °C by handheld IR. HF-300 bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface, with documented limits of normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is therefore 15 °C above normal, 5 °C above the alarm limit and 5 °C below trip. Because it is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, the applicable site response is a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration of 2.5 mm/s is numerically within Figure 3 Zone A, 0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, labelled 'New machines'; it is 0.3 mm/s below the Zone A/B boundary at 2.8 mm/s RMS. It is not in Zone C, 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS, or Zone D, 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS. This classification is provisional because Figure 3 applies to RMS velocity measured on bearing housings, while the report does not state RMS or provide readings from both housings; the manual requires classification of the highest reading from both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current readings do not establish an immediate-stop condition: 85 °C is below the 90 °C trip, and 2.5 mm/s is not in the manufacturer's highest vibration severity zone. The site's immediate-stop rule applies to Zone D vibration; it does not replace the separate P1 response required for the temperature alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — check first as a manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. No grease quantity or condition is reported, so this remains unconfirmed; the evidence does not provide a numerical likelihood ranking of the causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — another manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Inspect the bearings; if bearing replacement is required, section 5.3 requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment — another manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Check alignment using section 5.4; its documented tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Respond within the shift as P1. Confirm and record the drive-end bearing-housing surface temperature and compare it with the 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip limits; do not treat the current 85 °C reading as already being at trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Repeat the vibration survey as velocity RMS on both bearing housings, recording each location and value. Classify the highest reading using Figure 3 and act on that zone. If the highest reading is in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot the high bearing temperature by checking grease quantity, inspecting bearing condition and checking alignment. Record the as-found grease condition, bearing findings and alignment measurements before confirming any replacement scope; do not invent a grease acceptance quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any internal pump or seal work, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. Follow the back pull-out design rather than disturbing casing or pipework unnecessarily.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly must be removed, treat it as a 68 kg lift. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment, because the assembly exceeds the site's 25 kg threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-replacement hold point: apply section 5.3 using the inspection findings. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature requiring replacement, replace both bearings as a pair — drive-end HF3-512, bearing 6312-C3, and non-drive-end HF3-510, bearing 6310-C3 — rather than replacing only the drive-end bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For reassembly of disturbed non-seal fasteners, use Table 5 values for lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; M16 casing bolts 210 Nm if the casing is opened; and M24 impeller nut 160 Nm if removed. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened. If seal work is separately added, do not use the manual's 25 Nm gland torque for this serial: HF3-450B and 30 Nm apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to service, maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry. Repeat the housing-surface temperature and both-housing vibration checks and compare them with the same temperature and vibration-zone criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; conditional on bearing-pair replacement being confirmed. Section 5.3 requires replacement together with the non-drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; conditional on bearing-pair replacement being confirmed and required together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on the casing being opened, and mandatory replacement whenever that occurs.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For lifting the 68 kg back pull-out assembly or any other component heavier than 25 kg: lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Chemical dosing status is not stated in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent measurement places vibration in Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run the mechanical seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement allowance: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians. Confirm the replacement scope before treating this as a committed total.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser-alignment allowance after work moving the motor or bearing housing: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland-torque conflict: the manual parts list and Table 5 specify component seal HF3-450 and M10 seal-gland nuts at 25 Nm, whereas SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-109 is serial HF3-23500 and is therefore within the bulletin range, so the bulletin governs any seal work on this asset: use HF3-450B, apply 30 Nm, and do not perform the superseded sleeve measurement for seal setting. The bulletin also requires shaft sleeve HF3-455 replacement if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Other Table 5 torques remain applicable. The current high-temperature report, with no leakage reported, does not itself establish that seal replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 2.5 mm/s vibration an RMS velocity, and which bearing housing or housings were measured? Readings from both housings and the highest value are needed for a definitive Figure 3 classification. [C06, C07]",
    "What are the specified and as-found bearing grease quantities? The troubleshooting table requires a grease-quantity check but provides no acceptance quantity or grease specification. [C09]",
    "What are the bearing inspection results and measured parallel and angular alignment values? These are needed to confirm whether bearing-pair replacement or corrective alignment is required. [C09, C10]",
    "What exact disassembly scope is required — bearing housing, back pull-out assembly, casing or impeller? This determines whether the lifting controls, casing gasket and conditional fastener torques apply. [C01, C02, C05, C10, C11, C15]",
    "Is the pump line chemically dosed? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory. [C15]",
    "Is there any confirmed reason to add mechanical-seal work despite no leakage being reported? If seal work is added, revise the parts and labour scope, apply HF3-450B at 30 Nm, and measure sleeve scoring to determine whether it exceeds 0.1 mm; the standard seal-replacement labour allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. [C09, C12, C13]",
    "What labour allowance should be assigned to the initial temperature verification, vibration survey, grease check and inspection? Table 6 provides standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment. [C12]"
  ]
}
